A simple PHP-website for file uploads without security measures. Requirements:
- upload.php must be owned by www-data
  - chown www-data:www-data upload.php
- /etc/php/<VERSION>/apache2/php.ini needs to have uploads activated

Additional CTF:
- Host upload.php on a Webserver (LAMP-Stack)
- "Hide" a file named "capture_me" with the flag-ID somewhere in /var/www-Folder
- Students have to
  - Configure php-Shell file to their attacker machine
  - Upload the shell.php
  - Start a listener on their attacker machine
  - Establish a reverse shell by GET shell.php
  - Find the flag: find / -type f -name "capture_me" 2>/dev/null
